======================================================================================
REG-009 §4 · THE PRE-COMMITTED STOPPING RULE, APPLIED
======================================================================================
Declared BEFORE this probe was written: if no band width achieves a §4.4
recovery probability above 0.80 while leaving at least 30 firm-years per band,
the delta design is REFUSED and P0's table is the result.
Evaluated on the firm-year-weighted recovery across bands that clear the 30
floor; the worst single band is printed beside it so a mean cannot hide one.

ERRATUM, RECORDED AND NOT REPAIRED. The rule as written prices RECOVERY and
the THIN floor and says nothing about COVERAGE -- the share of firm-years
living in bands that clear the floor. It is therefore satisfied by a width
that recovers well on a quarter of the sample. Coverage is printed in every
row below and in the sweep above; the verdict is computed on the rule AS
WRITTEN, because rewriting a pre-commitment after seeing the table is the one
move a pre-commitment exists to prevent (REG-002 E1's precedent: the defect
is recorded, the number is left unambiguous).
